From baf2d311203920ec79663737fb727fe7f3bcf6e4 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Seuj09 <jeus110310@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 21:46:17 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] Input: add OmniVision TCM SPI touchscreen driver (host
 download)

Add a driver for OmniVision TCM touch controllers that have no flash and come
up in a ROM bootloader after every reset. The host downloads an HDL firmware
image with request_firmware(), runs it, answers the APP_CONFIG, DISPLAY and
OPENSHORT requests, then reads the application info and registers a
multitouch input device. A panel reset also resets the controller; the driver
notices the new ROM-boot identify report and downloads again.

It is written from how the stock omnivision_tcm driver behaves on the wire
rather than copied from it. Not implemented: the older F35/RMI download path,
flash update, diagnostics and gestures.

Signed-off-by: Seuj09 <jeus110310@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/input/touchscreen/Kconfig       | 1444 +++++++++++++++++++++++
 drivers/input/touchscreen/Makefile      |  123 ++
 drivers/input/touchscreen/ovt-tcm-spi.c | 1163 ++++++++++++++++++
 3 files changed, 2730 insertions(+)
 create mode 100644 drivers/input/touchscreen/Kconfig
 create mode 100644 drivers/input/touchscreen/Makefile
 create mode 100644 drivers/input/touchscreen/ovt-tcm-spi.c

